// A module that declares only TYPES. `vl check` returns 0 — "Checked 1 file, no errors." —
// and `vl build` refuses with `emitProgram: expected at least one top-level function or
// statement` (`compiler/emit_sections.vl:3881`). Nothing to print: a declarations-only module
// lowers to an empty wasm module, so this probe passes when it merely BUILDS AND RUNS.
//
// THE REFUSAL IS ABOUT THE ENTRY POSITION ONLY, and that is what makes it a capability gap
// rather than a design rule. The identical file IMPORTED by a program that uses `Point`
// compiles and runs today; it is refused only when it is the file being built. So the compiler
// already agrees a types-only module is a legal module — it just cannot be the one you name.
//
// THE EMPTY FILE IS A DIFFERENT SITE. Zero bytes fires `emitProgram: expected at least one
// top-level statement` (`emit_sections.vl:4394`), which reaches the arena-root check before
// the pass table runs. Do not conflate the two: this probe needs a declaration present.
//
// EVERY DECLARATION FORM REPRODUCES IT — a struct type, a scalar alias, an `export`ed type.
// One is enough here; the family is recorded in the inventory row.
//
// Either resolution closes it: emit the empty module, or move the diagnosis into the CHECKER
// (a `loud emit reject` is a clause-2 violation by construction, since `check` returned 0 to
// reach the emitter — either the program is legal and should compile, or the checker owed the
// diagnosis).
export type Point = { x: i32, y: i32 }
